exam: A total of {s} {t} is distributed among three bags. It is given that the first bag contains {p} {t} and that the second contains {d} {t} in excess of the first. Determine the number of {t} contained in the third bag.
exam: A rope of {s} metres is divided into three pieces, whereof the first measures {p} metres and the second exceeds the first by {d} metres. Ascertain the length, in metres, of the third piece.
exam: Whereas the sum of three quantities is {s}, the first being {p} and the second exceeding the first by {d}, state the value of the third quantity.
exam: Compute the number of {t} remaining for the third pupil, given that {s} {t} are apportioned among three pupils, the first receiving {p} and the second receiving {d} more than the first.
exercise: Great-aunt Edna passed away and left {s} dollars to her three nephews. The first got {p} dollars, and the second got {d} dollars more than the first. How many dollars did the third get?
exercise: Dad was made redundant and got {s} dollars to go. He paid {p} dollars of bills, then {d} dollars more than that on the car, and the rest went into savings. How many dollars went into savings?
